※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4030
※ pl4g-test: args -shared
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4030 LANG_HOST_TEXT_MADE_ELSEWHERE

※ The text a host answers is copied, before the call returns, into room of
※ the program's own, and that room is the heap's: the host is handed no arena
※ to copy into, and the image is nowhere to copy anything to.  So `in ⎕heap`
※ may be said of it, which is what saying nothing says, and nothing else.

@[host("in_an_arena")]
fn in_an_arena(pool: &mut arena) → str in pool

@[host("in_the_image")]
fn in_the_image() → str in ⎕static

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn run() → i64:
    0i64
